Package: psyWiz
Type: Package
Title: Psychometric Wizardry for Scales and Factor Models
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Herman", "Elgueta", email = "herman.elgueta@umag.cl", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6764-5490"))
Description: Tools for scale psychometrics built on 'lavaan', usable from R
    and as a 'jamovi' module. Checks one scale (reliability, tests of
    tau-equivalence and parallelism, Guttman and Mokken scalability); tests
    measurement invariance across groups step by step for continuous and for
    ordinal items (Wu & Estabrook, 2016), with verdicts, score tests for the
    worst-fitting constraints and a multiverse check of the verdicts; compares
    estimators, and confirmatory against exploratory structural equation
    models, side by side; and checks whether formative indicators act through
    a single composite. Independent models are fitted on several processor
    cores when that saves time.
License: GPL-3
URL: https://github.com/heelgueta/psywiz
BugReports: https://github.com/heelgueta/psywiz/issues
